-   refer parasite.Supervisor
+   refer parasite.Supervisor

-   entry .platformThreads   each task on a new platform thread: `PlatformSupervisor`
-   entry .virtualThreads   each task on a virtual thread: `VirtualSupervisor`
-       Needs Java 21 and fails at runtime on an older JVM; forks platform threads on Scala
-       Native, where there is no Loom.
-   entry .adaptiveThreads   virtual threads where the JVM has them, platform threads otherwise: `AdaptiveSupervisor`
-   entry .pooledThreads   tasks on reusable carrier threads: `PooledSupervisor`
-       For fine-grained fan-out, where a thread start per task would dominate; a task has no
-       thread of its own, so thread-locals persist across the tasks a carrier runs.
-   entry .javascriptThreads   tasks run eagerly at their fork, on one strand: `JavascriptSupervisor`
-       The model for Scala.js, with the limits of a single strand: no interleaving, instant
-       sleeps, and a panic on a wait which no completed task could ever end.
+   entry .platformThreads   ogni task su un nuovo platform thread: `PlatformSupervisor`
+   entry .virtualThreads   ogni task su un virtual thread: `VirtualSupervisor`
+       Richiede Java 21 e fallisce a runtime su una JVM più vecchia; su Scala Native, dove non
+       c'è Loom, crea platform thread.
+   entry .adaptiveThreads   virtual thread dove la JVM li ha, platform thread altrimenti: `AdaptiveSupervisor`
+   entry .pooledThreads   task su thread portatori riutilizzabili: `PooledSupervisor`
+       Per il fan-out a grana fine, dove l'avvio di un thread per task dominerebbe; un task non
+       ha un thread proprio, quindi i thread-local persistono attraverso i task che un
+       portatore esegue.
+   entry .javascriptThreads   task eseguiti subito al loro fork, su un unico trefolo: `JavascriptSupervisor`
+       Il modello per Scala.js, con i limiti di un unico trefolo: nessuna intercalazione,
+       pause istantanee, e un panic su un'attesa che nessun task completato potrebbe mai
+       terminare.

